        <mxCell id="n1" value="&lt;b&gt;SSD-B7 with B8: Confirm handover, return and complete&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Document:&lt;/b&gt; behaviour design, step A9 (S3)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Version:&lt;/b&gt; 1.0; &lt;b&gt;Date:&lt;/b&gt; 2026-10-11&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Author:&lt;/b&gt; Student 3 (S3), drafted with Claude; reviewed by: ______&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Status:&lt;/b&gt; Draft for design gate A14&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Based on:&lt;/b&gt; Use Cases v1.3 (UC-B7, UC-B8), FR/NFR v1.3&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Package:&lt;/b&gt; Module 3 (borrowing lifecycle)" style="rounded=0;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#999999;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=8;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="10" y="10" width="400" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2" value="&lt;b&gt;FRs realised:&lt;/b&gt; FR-B-11, FR-B-12 (UC-B7); FR-B-13, FR-B-14, FR-B-15 (UC-B8).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rationale:&lt;/b&gt; The two use cases share one diagram because the handover ends in ACTIVE and the return starts from it, which puts the dual-confirmation rule of FR-B-11 and FR-B-13 in one place. Each party's confirmation is its own system event (the par frame), and COMPLETED is reported only after both have confirmed, with the deposit release recorded and never moved. A dispute raised from either use case is a ref to SSD-B12 rather than a second copy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Not shown:&lt;/b&gt; UC-B7 *a (no handover action, then NO_SHOW) and UC-B8 *a (overdue, then automatic dispute) are scheduler jobs (B13), not actor events." style="rounded=0;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#999999;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=8;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="420" y="10" width="440" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n3" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt; (UML 2.5.1 sequence notation; SSD convention after Larman)&lt;br&gt;Stick figure: actor outside the system. Box: the system as one black box, no internals.&lt;br&gt;Solid line, filled head: system event. Dashed line, open head: return. Solid line, open head: asynchronous notification.&lt;br&gt;alt / opt / par / ref: combined fragments. Replies that carry no data are omitted. Numbers follow the use case steps; the right margin gives the step or extension." style="rounded=0;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;html=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=8;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="870" y="10" width="330" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
